    fix(gate): tier-1 secrets stops grading gitignored bytecode (CF-383)
    
    `gitleaks detect --no-git` — the tier-1 secrets step — scans the WORKING TREE, so it also
    graded a file git can never commit:
    
        RuleID: private-key   Entropy: 4.74
        File:   tests/__pycache__/test_node_provisioning.cpython-314.pyc
        Line:   35
    
    Those bytes are the synthetic PEM fixture `tests/test_node_provisioning.py` writes to prove a
    0644 deploy key is refused; there is no secret in the tree. Bytecode is already gitignored
    (`__pycache__/`, `*.pyc`) and the commit guard scans staged files only, so the guard reported
    clean while the judge failed the same tree: verdict c46e82aa failed CF-003 with lint PASS,
    tests PASS and tier-2 PASS.
    
    `.gitleaks.toml` `[allowlist].paths` now carries the two bytecode entries, `'''__pycache__/'''`
    and `'''\.pyc$'''`, with a comment naming the reason. They drop the generated path tier-1 was
    reading and nothing else: every existing entry is kept, and since an excluded path can never be
    committed, the exclusion cannot hide a real key. Measured: the tier-1 command now scans 2.96 MB
    instead of 3.93 MB and prints `no leaks found` with exit 0.
    
    `tests/selftest.sh` section 34 carries the arm that owns the property — three arms over one
    scratch tree: GREEN (a PEM inside `tests/__pycache__/fixture.cpython-314.pyc` yields no finding,
    with a graded anchor so a clean run cannot be a scan that read nothing), CONTROL (the same PEM
    outside `__pycache__` is still reported, so the exclusion is scoped and not a mute), and
    LOAD-BEARING (the same tree with the two entries stripped from a copy of the config IS reported,
    so deleting them turns the arm red). A host without gitleaks prints a named SKIP, never a silent
    pass. Mutation-checked before commit: deleting the entries reds arm 1 only; widening the
    allowlist to `.*\.py` reds all three (`scanned ~0 bytes`, the anti-vacuity guard).
    
    Traceability: `docs/handbook/chapters/M3-repository.md` §3 S3 row, §5 settings register and §7
    verification table each name the bytecode exclusion and record that tier-1 grades the working
    tree while the commit guard grades staged files — finding
    `tests/__pycache__/test_node_provisioning.cpython-314.pyc:35`, rule `private-key`, 2026-11-07.
